olish-ukrainian-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Polish–Ukrainian War</span><span class="enc-type">War · 1918–1919</span><span class="enc-snip">The Polish–Ukrainian War was fought from November 1918 to July 1919 over Eastern Galicia, after the collapse of Austria-Hungary.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/politburo"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/politburo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Politburo</span><span class="enc-type">Institution</span><span class="enc-snip">The Politburo (Political Bureau) is the executive committee of a communist party's Central Committee and the real centre of power in a communist state.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/politics-aristotle"><span class="enc-name">Politics (Aristotle)</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">Politics is a treatise on government by the Greek philosopher Aristotle, written in the fourth century BCE.</span></a></li></ul>
